ec­\ntion 32 of the Trading with the Enemy \nAct, the Attorney General shall carry \nout the functions provided for in that \nsubsection, including the powers, duties, \nauthority and discretion thereby vested \nin or conferred upon the President; and \nfunctions under the said subsection are \nhereby delegated to the Attorney Gen­\neral, and the Attorney General is hereby \ndesignated thereunder, accordingly.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"20 FR 361, PDF pages 1-1; Sec. 2","sha256":"47e31602eedbeaf9b9af41557086913025e35a316ec96c6c670f0320a038aefa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1955-01-15/pdf/FR-1955-01-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10587#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. The Attorney General may del­\negate to any officer and agency of the \nDepartment of Justice such of his func­\ntions under this order as he may deem \nnecessary.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"20 FR 361, PDF pages 1-1; Sec. 3","sha256":"47e31602eedbeaf9b9af41557086913025e35a316ec96c6c670f0320a038aefa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1955-01-15/pdf/FR-1955-01-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:10587#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"20 FR 361, PDF pages 1-1","sha256":"47e31602eedbeaf9b9af41557086913025e35a316ec96c6c670f0320a038aefa","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1955-01-15/pdf/FR-1955-01-15.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 3 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","i